    board: file CF-153 — the create path cannot honour the remedy its own error prints
    
    scripts/node-create.sh has no --ref flag and forwards no ref, so the node-side
    remedy it prints (`ref 'main' was not found; pass --ref <branch-or-tag>`) is a
    flag the only documented create command rejects with `unknown arg: --ref`.
    
    Measured on a clean clone of origin/main c29c024 (arms re-checked against
    f26a608; git diff --name-only -- scripts/ README.md = 0 files between them), and
    re-run unchanged after rebinding onto 23c1c6d, the sibling's CF-126 fix:
    
      BUNKER_SERVER=no-such-server bash scripts/node-create.sh --project p \
        --repo https://github.com/git/git --harness hermes --ref master
      -> unknown arg: --ref   rc=2
    
      HOME=$(mktemp -d) bash scripts/project-node.sh --apply --layers 40 \
        --project refproof --repo https://github.com/git/git
      -> FAIL  repo_clone — ref 'main' was not found; pass --ref <branch-or-tag>
    
    README.md:80-81 offers `--ref <branch>` as what a non-main default branch needs;
    project-node.sh:33/:53 support it; node-create.sh:56-67 has no such flag and :103
    forwards only NODE_PROJECT and NODE_GATEWAY_PORT, so NODE_REF cannot cross either.
    
    Filing only: the repair is future work tracked by the pending row, not in this
    commit. This diff touches the board and one audit file; no script and no README,
    so the CF-126 fix on the base commit is unaffected by it.
    
    Walked under the family barrier (sibling lane code-factory status=running) from a
    throwaway clone; the dirty candidate checkout was never read or written, and no
    agent was spawned (the probe pins a nonexistent server).
    
    Addresses: CF-153
